        "abstract": "<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>Given an integer m\u2a7e2 and rational numbers A1,\u2026, Am, u1,\u2026, Um not all zero, we obtain a rational sequence using the linear recurrence relation, [eq] Sequences of this kind have been studied extensively and the theory has a long and colourful history. One of the earliest and best known is the Fibonacci sequence. This begins u1 = u2 = 1, and continues via the recurrence relation A slightly more exotic example occurs with the problem of the man who walks along an infinite ladder.</jats:p>",
